# Ship AI SaaS Starter — AI assistant rules

Context for Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code and friends. Read this before writing
code in this repo; it exists so you generate imports that resolve and patterns
that match the rest of the codebase.

## Stack

Next.js 16 (App Router) · React 19 · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS v4 · shadcn/ui ·
Drizzle ORM on Postgres · Better-Auth · Stripe · Resend · Vercel AI SDK ·
Contentlayer (MDX) · Zustand.

## Layout

```
app/(marketing)/        public pages       app/(docs)/        help centre
app/(app)/(auth)/       login, signup      app/(app)/(protected)/  dashboard, admin
app/api/chat/           chat + history     app/api/tasks/generate/  task runner
config/                 ai, tasks, subscriptions, site, dashboard
lib/ai/                 chat.ts, structured.ts, models.ts
lib/db/                 index.ts, schema/, migrations/
lib/auth.ts             Better-Auth setup  lib/auth/middleware.ts   withAuth wrapper
lib/utils/usage.ts      updateUsage, checkRateLimits
```

Import with the `@/` alias: `import { db } from "@/lib/db"`.

## Rules that matter

### Database

- Schema lives in `lib/db/schema/account.ts` (users, teams, usage) and
  `lib/db/schema/chat.ts` (conversations, messages). Add new tables in that
  folder and export them from the schema barrel in `lib/db/index.ts`.
- Every tenant-scoped table has a `teamId`. Always filter by it — a query
  without a team filter is a data leak.
- After changing schema: `npm run db:generate` then `npm run db:migrate`.
  Never hand-edit files in `lib/db/migrations/`.
- Use Drizzle's query builder (`db.query.x.findMany`, `db.select()`), not raw SQL.

### Auth

- API routes use the `withAuth` wrapper from `lib/auth/middleware.ts`, which
  injects `{ req, user, team, routeParams }`. Do not re-implement session
  checks inside a route.
- Server components and actions use `getCurrentUser()` / `getCurrentTeam()`
  from `lib/auth/actions.ts`.
- This starter is single-workspace: one team per user, created by the
  `databaseHooks.user.create.after` hook in `lib/auth.ts`. There are no
  invitations, no member management and no org-level roles.
- App-level roles (`user`, `admin`, `superadmin`) gate `/admin` through
  `proxy.ts`.

### AI

- All chat goes through `streamChat()` in `lib/ai/chat.ts`. One `streamText`
  call, one persistence path.
- Structured responses use `generateText` with `Output.object` from
  `lib/ai/structured.ts`. **Never use `generateObject`.**
- Models are declared in `lib/ai/models.ts` and resolved with `resolveModel()`.
  Do not instantiate a provider client anywhere else.
- The system prompt belongs in `config/ai.ts`, not inline in a route.
- There are no tools, agents or background workflows in this starter. Do not
  invent imports for them.

### Usage and limits

- Every AI entry point calls `checkRateLimits()` **before** the model call and
  `updateUsage()` after it (both from `lib/utils/usage.ts`).
- One chat message or task run counts as one request. Limits per plan live in
  `config/subscriptions.ts`.

### UI

- Use existing shadcn/ui components from `components/ui/` before adding new ones.
- **Theme tokens only.** Never write hardcoded palette classes like
  `bg-blue-500`, `text-gray-900`, `text-emerald-400` or inline hex colours. Use
  `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-muted`, `bg-primary`, `bg-destructive`,
  `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border`, `ring`, and
  `chart-1`…`chart-5`, all defined in `styles/globals.css`.
- Client components need `"use client"`. Keep data fetching in server
  components or route handlers where you can.
- Global client state uses Zustand stores in `stores/`.

### General

- TypeScript everywhere; no new `.js` files.
- Prefer editing an existing file over creating a parallel one.
- Match the surrounding comment density and naming. This is a starter people
  read to learn the codebase — clarity beats cleverness.
